# Chained data transformation
# Demonstrates nested implicit map — the core eric-lang pattern.
#
# In the principled rewrite, each print is sequenced through an IO monad.
# Side effects are pure. Referential transparency is maintained.
# (The original implementation used eval() on raw Python strings.)

("1\n2\n3", "4\n5\n6", "7\n8\n9")
    split("\n")
        int
    sum
print
